00:57:51,081 --> 00:57:52,816
Be careful.

506
00:57:52,816 --> 00:57:54,784
Go, go! All right.

507
00:58:21,311 --> 00:58:23,939
Wow! Take it.
Wow, so much food!

508
00:58:42,833 --> 00:58:45,165
Sashke, are you asleep?

509
00:58:51,508 --> 00:58:53,476
Sashke, where are you?

510
00:58:53,476 --> 00:58:55,412
Hey, stop.
Guys!!! Jiggers!

511
00:58:55,412 --> 00:58:57,247
Let's take off, boys.

512
00:58:57,247 --> 00:59:00,750
Hey, you gang, stop. l'll shot.
l said stay. Where are you going? Stay.

513
00:59:00,750 --> 00:59:03,275
Sashke!

514
00:59:14,664 --> 00:59:15,858
Your name and your last name?

515
00:59:26,243 --> 00:59:29,508
lt means your name is a thief and l will
send you to the prison, do you understand?

516
00:59:30,847 --> 00:59:32,549
My name is Sabyr.

517
00:59:32,549 --> 00:59:33,709
Sabyr?

518
00:59:36,186 --> 00:59:39,856
May my eyes get poked,
if you are Sabyr! Sabyr!

519
00:59:39,856 --> 00:59:42,993
That is true, ask Kasym.

520
00:59:42,993 --> 00:59:44,995
Which Kasym?

521
00:59:44,995 --> 00:59:47,759
One-eyed rail track man.

522
00:59:48,965 --> 00:59:52,128
Track man. . .

523
00:59:54,104 --> 00:59:56,902
Don't cry! Eat the apple.

524
00:59:57,607 --> 00:59:59,632
Thanks, l hate them!

525
01:00:01,144 --> 01:00:04,045
You hate them! Stop crying now.

526
01:00:05,715 --> 01:00:09,082
We'll go and see who is going to
defend you this time!

527
01:00:11,087 --> 01:00:12,281
Understand?! Go! Go ahead.

528
01:00:14,157 --> 01:00:15,522
Let's go.

529
01:00:52,662 --> 01:00:55,131
Thank you very much!

530
01:00:55,131 --> 01:01:00,660
Hey! Lift up your eyes. Look here.

531
01:01:02,372 --> 01:01:06,910
Listen to me: when you are leaving,

532
01:01:06,910 --> 01:01:09,902
tell me where you are going and why.

533
01:01:10,981 --> 01:01:15,213
Do you understand?

534
01:01:16,019 --> 01:01:17,452
Yes.

535
01:01:20,090 --> 01:01:21,785
You put me to shame.

536
01:01:45,281 --> 01:01:47,909
Keepyatok, do you want more?

537
01:01:49,486 --> 01:01:50,885
You had enough.

538
01:01:52,922 --> 01:01:55,686
We are the same.

539
01:01:57,394 --> 01:02:00,852
You got left alone and l lost my parents.

540
01:02:05,502 --> 01:02:09,131
lt's OK, l will find them one day.

541
01:02:26,356 --> 01:02:27,791
Catch him. Throw higher.

542
01:02:27,791 --> 01:02:30,593
Give the money.

543
01:02:30,593 --> 01:02:32,424
Take care of it.
Yes, sir.

544
01:02:38,701 --> 01:02:40,293
Here you go.

545
01:02:43,073 --> 01:02:44,870
Where are you?
Here, Comrade Major!

546
01:02:56,119 --> 01:02:57,916
Quick, quick, quick.

547
01:03:01,624 --> 01:03:02,989
Please, Comrad Major.

548
01:03:10,867 --> 01:03:13,893
Kasym Batyrbaev, railroad man, local. . .

549
01:03:14,437 --> 01:03:17,770
A war participant. . .

550
01:03:26,883 --> 01:03:30,979
Animal.

551
01:03:33,056 --> 01:03:35,358
Babi, do you sell animals?

552
01:03:35,358 --> 01:03:37,724
We need all kind of animals. . .

553
01:03:39,395 --> 01:03:40,530
Ha!? Deaf, are you?

554
01:03:40,530 --> 01:03:41,792
He is contused.

555
01:03:44,501 --> 01:03:48,665
We are no confiscating, we are paying.

556
01:03:49,572 --> 01:03:55,204
For a big government thing.
A gift for Comrad Stalin's anniversary.

557
01:03:57,080 --> 01:04:02,785
Comrade Major, he is absolutely lonely. . .
in our words..

558
01:04:02,785 --> 01:04:07,620
Horsy- morsey! Are you a police, ha?

559
01:04:10,693 --> 01:04:13,429
Are you a part of the family?

560
01:04:13,429 --> 01:04:17,593
l know, you are all relatives. . .

561
01:04:18,968 --> 01:04:22,665
And you relative,
are you selling an animal?

562
01:04:34,584 --> 01:04:36,882
A Turtle, like a lemon!

563
01:04:41,758 --> 01:04:43,350
Whose is this Abraham?

564
01:04:47,397 --> 01:04:49,126
Perfect looking Kazakh!

565
01:04:51,134 --> 01:04:52,863
Where did you get him?

566
01:04:53,903 --> 01:04:55,461
l gave a birth to him!

567
01:04:56,639 --> 01:05:00,234
You? From whom?

568
01:05:01,511 --> 01:05:03,172
l wish l knew. . .

569
01:05:05,982 --> 01:05:08,644
May be there from Balgabai, ha!

570
01:05:15,758 --> 01:05:18,158
All right. . . A brave woman. . .

571
01:05:19,529 --> 01:05:23,090
Good for her.

572
01:05:28,037 --> 01:05:29,231
Let's go!

573
01:05:37,013 --> 01:05:39,106
Wait! Wait!

574
01:05:39,882 --> 01:05:41,213
Stop!

575
01:05:43,486 --> 01:05:45,655
Take him for free. . .

576
01:05:45,655 --> 01:05:49,921
Just make sure let Comrade Stalin know
that it is from me, Sabyr Povzner!

577
01:05:54,330 --> 01:05:55,297
Let's go!

578
01:06:02,105 --> 01:06:04,505
Let him my parents go free. . .

579
01:06:10,546 --> 01:06:12,377
Grandpa Kasym. . .

580
01:06:14,250 --> 01:06:18,788
lf we knew if Comrade Stalin
would like my gift or not. . .

581
01:06:18,788 --> 01:06:19,948
Yes.

582
01:06:20,823 --> 01:06:26,261
When l was like you Sashka. . .
l walked long ways. . .

583
01:06:27,196 --> 01:06:30,688
to a far winter place.

584
01:06:33,803 --> 01:06:39,909
l remember. . .throughout the steeps. . .
we put yurts. . .

585
01:06:39,909 --> 01:06:41,678
big celebration. . .

586
01:06:41,678 --> 01:06:47,016
Wedding! Thousands guess, can you imagine?
Lots of food, many games. . .

587
01:06:47,016 --> 01:06:49,552
Our tribe was the most respected.

588
01:06:49,552 --> 01:06:52,121
Many horses, camels. . .

589
01:06:52,121 --> 01:06:57,560
Catching a girl! lt's a game. You have to
catch a girl. . . l caught up with one. . .

590
01:06:57,560 --> 01:07:00,196
and kissed her.

591
01:07:00,196 --> 01:07:01,197
And then?

592
01:07:01,197 --> 01:07:05,902
A wedding then! We had three children!

593
01:07:05,902 --> 01:07:07,637
And then?

594
01:07:07,637 --> 01:07:12,942
Then hunger, . . . no one stayed alive.

595
01:07:12,942 --> 01:07:15,172
And then?

596
01:07:15,978 --> 01:07:18,548
A war came then.

597
01:07:18,548 --> 01:07:20,709
And then what?

598
01:07:21,184 --> 01:07:24,449
And then l had you.

599
01:07:25,922 --> 01:07:27,446
Oh, Allah. . .

600
01:07:53,049 --> 01:07:54,448
Listen,

601
01:07:58,388 --> 01:08:07,126
l am alone and you are alone. . .
We are both alone here forever. . .

602
01:08:10,833 --> 01:08:15,566
Let's, how do you say it. . .

603
01:08:17,940 --> 01:08:20,101
well, live together, ha?

604
01:08:23,079 --> 01:08:26,879
Like a husband and a wife. . .

605
01:08:28,551 --> 01:08:30,985
Would you feel.

606
01:08:57,513 --> 01:09:00,650
See, you cannot find like this anywhere!

607
01:09:00,650 --> 01:09:03,050
Wow, a shell!

608
01:09:03,619 --> 01:09:06,222
We have one like this in Moscow.

609
01:09:06,222 --> 01:09:09,055
lt says ''gagry'' on it.

610
01:09:10,059 --> 01:09:12,789
Mom and Dad brought it from the Black Sea.

611
01:09:13,296 --> 01:09:16,060
Was a sea here before, too?

612
01:09:16,766 --> 01:09:23,535
Everything was here before.
Once it seems there was a sea here.

613
01:09:24,674 --> 01:09:25,971
Here you go, son.

614
01:09:57,773 --> 01:10:01,209
Put it over there.

615
01:10:04,046 --> 01:10:06,981
Lay it down over there.

616
01:10:22,932 --> 01:10:29,238
Oh, God Almighty, give rest to
the innocent souls

617
01:10:29,238 --> 01:10:33,698
and may the land be like a feather
for them. Amen.

618
01:10:43,352 --> 01:10:44,478
Here you go.

619
01:10:52,395 --> 01:10:54,386
A grandpa is here. . .

620
01:10:55,731 --> 01:10:57,892
Who is your God, Grandpa Kasym?

621
01:11:00,970 --> 01:11:06,108
God is one for everyone.
For me and for you.

622
01:11:06,108 --> 01:11:09,771
For Ezhi, for mom Vera,

623
01:11:10,446 --> 01:11:12,748
for Faty, for Gleb also?

624
01:11:12,748 --> 01:11:16,319
One for all. . . for all, son.

625
01:11:16,319 --> 01:11:18,588
What language does he speak?

626
01:11:18,588 --> 01:11:20,990
He knows all languages,

627
01:11:20,990 --> 01:11:26,792
the main thing is that the word
would come from the heart.

628
01:11:30,132 --> 01:11:34,737
Remember this spot, this land,

629
01:11:34,737 --> 01:11:40,476
someday you will return here, son.

630
01:11:40,476 --> 01:11:43,968
Why, are you going to send me somewhere?

631
01:11:49,385 --> 01:11:54,345
Hey, Kazakhs, move.
There is one more good news.

632
01:13:48,604 --> 01:13:51,732
Hey, you're thieves.
Go, go from here.

633
01:14:03,552 --> 01:14:10,760
Hey, how fat! lt would make good
''beshparmak'', enough for everyone.

634
01:14:10,760 --> 01:14:15,831
You have no fault, we have no food.

635
01:14:15,831 --> 01:14:17,433
The Almighty prepared you for us to eat.

636
01:14:17,433 --> 01:14:18,923
Amen.

637
01:14:25,241 --> 01:14:27,141
No, don't pick.

638
01:14:31,080 --> 01:14:33,382
Soooo. You have not eaten without me,
have you?

639
01:14:33,382 --> 01:14:38,581
What a good place.
Now you will be a healthy Kazak.

640
01:14:41,357 --> 01:14:45,094
Add more salt, the meat would be softer.

641
01:14:45,094 --> 01:14:46,095
Hey, be careful!

642
01:14:46,095 --> 01:14:48,029
Why are you closing?

643
01:15:12,054 --> 01:15:23,363
Hurrah! Bride and a groom!

644
01:15:25,000 --> 01:15:27,264
l bless you!!!

645
01:15:28,637 --> 01:15:29,899
Hey, Faty!

646
01:15:59,702 --> 01:16:05,641
This is a gift for you from the Koreans

647
01:16:05,641 --> 01:16:08,944
and Dungans of our region.

648
01:16:08,944 --> 01:16:10,741
Thank you.

649
01:16:11,146 --> 01:16:13,816
Sir, would you bless it?

650
01:16:13,816 --> 01:16:16,051
Good for you! Thanks!

651
01:16:16,051 --> 01:16:17,453
Finally, ''beshparmak'' is here!

652
01:16:17,453 --> 01:16:19,455
Thank you, dear. All the blessings to you.

653
01:16:19,455 --> 01:16:21,891
Dear guests, before a big feast
receive my blessings.

654
01:16:21,891 --> 01:16:24,193
Let the people have peace
and let the country have order.

655
01:16:24,193 --> 01:16:26,195
Happiness for the young. Amen.

656
01:16:26,195 --> 01:16:27,696
Amen!

657
01:16:27,696 --> 01:16:31,100
Here . . . the ears.

658
01:16:31,100 --> 01:16:33,302
Somebody will be lucky now!

659
01:16:33,302 --> 01:16:36,669
lt's for our Sashka so he can hear well.

660
01:16:38,140 --> 01:16:44,010
The eyes are for the polishman
so he can keep an eye on Verka.

661
01:16:45,014 --> 01:16:50,714
The neck - for Verka,
so you can turn around your Ezhi.

662
01:16:51,954 --> 01:16:55,391
This is for my friend Faty,
so he can well. . . .

663
01:16:55,391 --> 01:16:56,492
Speak, speak...

664
01:16:56,492 --> 01:16:57,857
No! Chat!

665
01:16:59,461 --> 01:17:00,758
Thanks!

666
01:17:12,174 --> 01:17:17,202
And now friends, let's take this toast
for the bride and the groom.

667
01:17:24,920 --> 01:17:37,526
Congratulation! Congratulation!

668
01:17:38,434 --> 01:17:45,074
A bright moon in a windless night,

669
01:17:45,074 --> 01:17:51,613
A light is blinking.

670
01:17:51,613 --> 01:17:59,655
A soul of a village is so deep,

671
01:17:59,655 --> 01:18:07,255
Like a roaring lake.

672
01:18:08,130 --> 01:18:09,927
Verka, shit. . .

673
01:18:12,901 --> 01:18:15,597
Dombrovskiy, get up!

674
01:18:16,939 --> 01:18:18,634
l said get up!

675
01:18:19,775 --> 01:18:20,935
Sit.

676
01:18:21,176 --> 01:18:23,440
What's the party is here!

677
01:18:25,714 --> 01:18:27,739
Verka, fuck you. . .

678
01:18:31,787 --> 01:18:32,287
Verka. . .

679
01:18:32,287 --> 01:18:35,424
Boys, run, a pistol. Run, quick.

680
01:18:35,424 --> 01:18:37,392
Verka, look at me!

681
01:18:37,960 --> 01:18:42,021
Handy Hoh, legs apart,
we are going to you!

682
01:18:45,134 --> 01:18:50,105
Sir, don't, stop it, we are relatives,

683
01:18:50,105 --> 01:18:52,674
don't shame me in front of people.

684
01:18:52,674 --> 01:18:54,943
What, what happened, what did l do?!

685
01:18:54,943 --> 01:18:57,571
Son of the bitch, you are an animal,
what relatives?

686
01:18:59,214 --> 01:19:05,380
You are putting me to shame
in front of the people.

687
01:19:06,955 --> 01:19:09,091
What are you doing, Kasym?
You are going crazy.

688
01:19:09,091 --> 01:19:14,396
You ashamed me in front of everyone,
crooked old man.

689
01:19:14,396 --> 01:19:23,305
l'll show you! l considered you as
a relative. You messed up my authority.

690
01:19:23,305 --> 01:19:26,968
Get up! Everyone in your compartments!

691
01:19:27,743 --> 01:19:30,268
Dombrovskjuy, shit!

692
01:19:36,018 --> 01:19:40,512
How did you dare to raise you hand? Shit.

693
01:19:41,156 --> 01:19:44,751
You raised your hand on the
Soviet authority, have you?

694
01:19:49,431 --> 01:19:56,269
This is for you, Mr. Dombrovskuy
from Balgabai.

695
01:19:56,705 --> 01:19:59,299
Let him go!!! Go away!

696
01:20:07,649 --> 01:20:11,380
Let me go!!!

697
01:20:37,479 --> 01:20:40,642
Let me go!!!

698
01:20:47,222 --> 01:20:48,416
Ezhik!

699
01:20:49,057 --> 01:20:54,825
Dear, what have you done?!
You killed the policeman!

700
01:21:10,078 --> 01:21:12,308
Verka,. . .

701
01:21:16,552 --> 01:21:18,287
l just. . . .

702
01:21:18,287 --> 01:21:20,949
What?

703
01:21:27,429 --> 01:21:38,073
Sir, l am not guilty, you saw, he himself. . .

704
01:21:38,073 --> 01:21:39,641
Son of the bitch. . .

705
01:21:39,641 --> 01:21:44,271
Ezhik!

706
01:21:45,247 --> 01:21:48,341
Come on, don't die! Ezhik!

707
01:21:49,351 --> 01:21:54,189
lt's not me, he himself. . .

708
01:21:54,189 --> 01:21:57,025
l knew it will finish like this.
Curse you!

709
01:21:57,025 --> 01:21:58,327
Get lost.

710
01:21:58,327 --> 01:22:02,431
Do not leave me, please! Do not leave me!
Dear. . . lt's not me, he himself. . .

711
01:22:02,431 --> 01:22:05,867
Open your eyes, dear, please.

712
01:22:05,867 --> 01:22:08,503
Ezhik!

713
01:22:08,503 --> 01:22:13,873
Lord! Then take me too!

714
01:23:46,968 --> 01:23:49,630
This is food for you.

715
01:24:17,733 --> 01:24:21,136
This is a picture of your parents.

716
01:24:21,136 --> 01:24:26,403
This is the address of your relatives.

717
01:24:27,242 --> 01:24:28,539
Do you understand?

718
01:24:29,344 --> 01:24:30,333
Yes.

719
01:24:33,615 --> 01:24:37,986
This is your grandfather's prayer book.

720
01:24:37,986 --> 01:24:41,683
Hey, are you scared?

721
01:24:42,457 --> 01:24:45,790
Remember, never be afraid of anything.

722
01:24:55,604 --> 01:24:58,835
Take care of yourself, grandpa Kasym.

723
01:25:04,679 --> 01:25:06,408
That's it. Let's go.

724
01:25:21,997 --> 01:25:25,467
How will you be without me?
l don't want to leave.

725
01:25:25,467 --> 01:25:28,904
Don't cry, son! Don't cry!
You are a man.

726
01:25:28,904 --> 01:25:31,031
l don't wanna leave, grandpa.

727
01:25:31,673 --> 01:25:34,437
Be happy, my son. Have a good trip.

728
01:25:35,343 --> 01:25:37,834
Have a good trip, son.

729
01:25:47,055 --> 01:25:51,822
Get up, get up!

730
01:26:04,906 --> 01:26:08,710
Be happy, son!

731
01:26:08,710 --> 01:26:13,443
Kasym grandpa. Take care of yourself.
l will come back.

732
01:26:17,452 --> 01:26:19,113
Have a good trip, my son.

733
01:26:28,563 --> 01:26:34,336
O, Almighty, if there is any fault,
forgive me.

734
01:26:34,336 --> 01:26:42,539
Give me faith, and happiness to my Sashka.

735
01:27:06,968 --> 01:27:09,037
Guys, we are attacked!

736
01:27:09,037 --> 01:27:11,028
Let me go!

737
01:27:11,206 --> 01:27:15,905
A police car came in the morning into the
village and arrested all the gang.

738
01:27:16,811 --> 01:27:20,713
They were suspected in organized order
of the policeman.

739
01:27:21,750 --> 01:27:25,053
Who shot Balgabai?

740
01:27:25,053 --> 01:27:29,717
Sultan? Gleb? Or somebody else?

741
01:27:33,094 --> 01:27:34,994
l could have been with them too

742
01:27:35,931 --> 01:27:41,164
if it was not for the old Kazakh man,
whom God enthrusted me to once.

743
01:28:33,822 --> 01:28:40,929
Many years later l found out that on August
29, 1 949, 1 70 kilometers from Semey,

744
01:28:40,929 --> 01:28:46,267
an atomic explosion took place for
the first time in the USSR.

745
01:28:46,267 --> 01:28:51,500
An anniversary gift for Stalin. . .

746
01:28:51,740 --> 01:28:57,078
A competition for the best children's
gift to our beloved

747
01:28:57,078 --> 01:29:01,947
Joseph Vissarionovich Stalin is taking
place all over our vast USSR homeland.

748
01:29:04,753 --> 01:29:08,623
And now Asembala Koibagarova will
sing a folk song by Abai,

749
01:29:08,623 --> 01:29:12,559
who is by the way from our land.

750
01:29:21,836 --> 01:29:27,142
A bright moon in a windless night,

751
01:29:27,142 --> 01:29:32,414
A light is blinking.

752
01:29:32,414 --> 01:29:38,687
A soul of a village is so deep,

753
01:29:38,687 --> 01:29:45,752
Like a roaring lake.

754
01:30:33,007 --> 01:30:42,450
This is the tree and there is nothing
around it. Only these bits of fabric.

755
01:30:42,450 --> 01:30:45,078
You can count how many people have been
under its branches.

756
01:30:46,488 --> 01:30:50,558
How many days l have waited to be here
again to humbly accept

757
01:30:50,558 --> 01:30:56,231
the past as the only and invaluable

758
01:30:56,231 --> 01:31:00,167
and happy life given to me by the fate.

759
01:31:00,635 --> 01:31:06,608
Here, among other lives the souls
of my grandfather,

760
01:31:06,608 --> 01:31:11,646
Kasym, of repenting Vera,
her husband polishman Ezhi,

761
01:31:11,646 --> 01:31:13,637
and restless Faty have found rest.

762
01:31:14,716 --> 01:31:16,911
May they rest in peace. . .

763
01:31:19,888 --> 01:31:23,688
l came back to call Kasym my father

764
01:31:24,359 --> 01:31:30,059
and devote to him the prayer which
is read in memory of parents.

765
01:31:38,006 --> 01:31:42,067
May His great name be blessed
forever and evere!

766
01:31:43,278 --> 01:31:47,374
May the name of the Holy One be blessed,

767
01:31:48,449 --> 01:31:52,620
uplifted, magnified and praised,

768
01:31:52,620 --> 01:31:56,257
His name is blessed above all blessings
and praise,

769
01:31:56,257 --> 01:32:00,057
and of all worship and comfort named
in the world!

770
01:32:01,496 --> 01:32:04,124
Let us say Amen!
